    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0505" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg423"/>

                <head>Mr. Montagnie to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 114.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nantes,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 16, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to report that the ship
                    which sailed yesterday from St. Nazaire to Vera Cruz carried four hundred
                    soldiers for the so-called emperor of Mexico. One hundred and fifty were French;
                    the rest belonged to the so-called “foreign legion.”</p>
                <p>I have the honor, sir, to remain, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN DE LA MONTAGNIÉ, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
